\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Fold-to-fold reproducibility across the five development folds: the most reproducible independently refitted classical selector in each case (Nogueira stability as primary ordering, mean pairwise Jaccard as tie-breaker), the two LLM hybrids whose final subset is fixed by a refitted statistical stage, and the pure LLM lists cached per fold on Home Credit and LendingClub. Jaccard is the mean pairwise Jaccard over the ten fold pairs; Min and Max are its minimum and maximum over the same pairs. $d$ is the Nogueira universe.}}{22}{table.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:stability}{{12}{22}{Fold-to-fold reproducibility across the five development folds: the most reproducible independently refitted classical selector in each case (Nogueira stability as primary ordering, mean pairwise Jaccard as tie-breaker), the two LLM hybrids whose final subset is fixed by a refitted statistical stage, and the pure LLM lists cached per fold on Home Credit and LendingClub. Jaccard is the mean pairwise Jaccard over the ten fold pairs; Min and Max are its minimum and maximum over the same pairs. $d$ is the Nogueira universe}{table.12}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Response sampling at a fixed prompt. Each row carries one cached semantic ranking's top $K$ through the frozen full-DEV pipeline to a single HO scoring run; the draws vary the cached response only and are not a confidence interval. Stability 2024 uses the ten repeated full-DEV calls of Section~\ref {subsec:stability_results}; Home Credit and LendingClub use the five rankings cached per fold partition over the identical candidate list. Spread is the range of held-out AUC over the draws, read against the materiality bar of $0.010$ (Section~\ref {subsec:inference}).}}{22}{table.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:response_spread}{{13}{22}{Response sampling at a fixed prompt. Each row carries one cached semantic ranking's top $\Kfeat $ through the frozen full-DEV pipeline to a single HO scoring run; the draws vary the cached response only and are not a confidence interval. Stability 2024 uses the ten repeated full-DEV calls of Section~\ref {subsec:stability_results}; Home Credit and LendingClub use the five rankings cached per fold partition over the identical candidate list. Spread is the range of held-out AUC over the draws, read against the materiality bar of $0.010$ (Section~\ref {subsec:inference})}{table.13}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Reproducibility landscape of fold-level selections. Orange: most reproducible refitted classical selector in each dataset--backbone case; green: pure LLM lists cached per fold on Home Credit and LendingClub. Circles are logistic regression ($K=20$), squares CatBoost ($K=40$). HC = Home Credit, LC = LendingClub v2, ST = Stability 2024. Higher is more reproducible on both axes; the dashed line marks equality of the two statistics. The Nogueira universe is the screened candidate set of the dataset for every point shown, so all points are on a common scale within a dataset; because the chance correction depends on $d$, values are not compared across datasets.}}{23}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:stability}{{3}{23}{Reproducibility landscape of fold-level selections. Orange: most reproducible refitted classical selector in each dataset--backbone case; green: pure LLM lists cached per fold on Home Credit and LendingClub. Circles are logistic regression ($\Kfeat =20$), squares CatBoost ($\Kfeat =40$). HC = Home Credit, LC = LendingClub v2, ST = Stability 2024. Higher is more reproducible on both axes; the dashed line marks equality of the two statistics. The Nogueira universe is the screened candidate set of the dataset for every point shown, so all points are on a common scale within a dataset; because the chance correction depends on $d$, values are not compared across datasets}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Name-obfuscation ablation on Home Credit. Held-out AUC of the pure LLM pipeline when the six ranking calls are repeated with the feature names replaced by seeded identifiers (arm A, definitions kept) or with the definitions removed (arm B, names kept), against the named cached rankings; same HO observations, same fixed backbones. Fold range is the span of the five fold-model AUCs. Overlap is the number of names the arm's subset shares with the named subset of the same partition and budget: for the full-DEV call (\ref {app:subsets}) and, as a range and mean, over the five fold calls. Ranks of the three external scores are given for the full-DEV call.}}{23}{table.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:obfuscation}{{14}{23}{Name-obfuscation ablation on Home Credit. Held-out AUC of the pure LLM pipeline when the six ranking calls are repeated with the feature names replaced by seeded identifiers (arm A, definitions kept) or with the definitions removed (arm B, names kept), against the named cached rankings; same HO observations, same fixed backbones. Fold range is the span of the five fold-model AUCs. Overlap is the number of names the arm's subset shares with the named subset of the same partition and budget: for the full-DEV call (\ref {app:subsets}) and, as a range and mean, over the five fold calls. Ranks of the three external scores are given for the full-DEV call}{table.14}{}}
